2026-09-16T19:35:12.023819+08:00  INFO ThreadId(01) longbridge_httpcli::request: http response duration=1.82836125s body={"code":0,"message":"success","data":{"items":[{"id":"299170048", "title":"Storage Chip Stocks Edge Up Premarket, MRAM Up 2.69%, WDC Gains 1.06%", "description":"Storage chip stocks traded mixed in premarket. MRAM(MRAM.US) led gains up 2.69%, WDC(WDC.US) rose 1.06%, while leveraged ETFs showed divergence.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299170048", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789555626"}, {"id":"299147744", "title":"Memory Chips Rise in Night Session, WDC Up 1.48%, MU Up 1.12%", "description":"Memory chip stocks rallied in the night session. Micron Technology rose 1.12% to $937.98, while Western Digital led major stocks with a 1.48% gain. SanDisk and Seagate Technology also advanced, with active trading across the sector.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299147744", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789544799"}, {"id":"299130581", "title":"Storage Chips Rise Broadly in Overnight Trading", "description":"Storage chip sector rose broadly in overnight trading on Sep 16. Mainstream stocks all gained, led by MRAM.US up 1.24%, followed by MU.US and WDC.US. Derivative products showed mixed performance, with MUD.US and SNDQ.US slightly down.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299130581", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789534047"}, {"id":"299128220", "title":"Trending | WDC Decreases 3% on Tuesday, Some Put options Soar 12100%", "description":"On September 15, Eastern Time, Western Digital options saw a total of 54696 contracts traded, with calls accounting for 50% and puts making up 49%.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299128220", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789532275"}, {"id":"299114651", "title":"Storage Chip Stocks Quiet in Overnight Trading, MRAM Up 0.69%, Micron Down 0.26%", "description":"Storage chip stocks showed mixed moves in overnight trading. MRAM led gains up 0.69%, while Micron(MU.US) fell 0.26% and SanDisk declined 0.33%. Most constituents moved less than 1%.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299114651", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789523256"}, {"id":"299101593", "title":"Storage Chip Stocks Edge Mixed in After-Hours, WDC Up 0.25%, MRAM Down 0.77%", "description":"Storage chip stocks traded mixed in after-hours. Western Digital(WDC.US) rose 0.25% to $413.00, Micron(MU.US) fell 0.18% to $925.89, SanDisk(SNDK.US) slipped 0.05% to $1530.20. Most constituents moved less than 1% as volume tapered.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299101593", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789512454"}, {"id":"299093493", "title":"Seagate Technology Holdings PLC Stock Underperforms Tuesday When Compared To Competitors", "description":"Seagate Technology Holdings PLC (STX) shares fell 4.19% to $771.81 on Tuesday, marking its fifth consecutive day of losses and underperforming competitors like NetApp and Western Digital. The stock closed 32.59% below its 52-week high. Trading volume was below the 50-day average. This decline occurred during a broader market downturn where the S&P 500 and Dow Jones also dropped.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299093493", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789504530"}, {"id":"299089928", "title":"Storage Chip Stocks Mixed in Trading, Seagate Down 4%, Western Digital Down 4%", "description":"Storage chip stocks traded mixed Tuesday. Seagate (STX.US) fell 4%, Western Digital (WDC.US) dropped 4%, while Micron (MU.US) edged up 0.20%. Leveraged ETF MUU gained 0.28%, inverse ETF SNDQ rose 2.31%.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299089928", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789501671"}, {"id":"299078683", "title":"Memory Chips Sector Declines During Trading Hours, STX Falls Nearly 5%, WDC Drops Over 3%", "description":"During trading hours on September 15, the memory chip sector weakened broadly, with Seagate Technology leading declines at nearly 5%, while Western Digital and SanDisk also retreated, with only SNDQ moving higher.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299078683", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789490786"}, {"id":"299076127", "title":"Western Digital Corp Stock (WDC) Moved Down by 3.00% on Sep 15: Drivers Behind the Movement", "description":"Western Digital Corp (WDC) stock fell 3.00% on Sep 15, underperforming the Technology Equipment sector. The decline was driven by broader semiconductor valuation reassessments, macroeconomic headwinds, and company-specific factors including convertible note redemptions causing dilution concerns and a discounted secondary SanDisk equity offering. Technical indicators show oversold conditions, while analysts maintain a 'Buy' rating with an average price target of $650.78.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299076127", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789489089"}, {"id":"299076620", "title":"Western Digital Stock (WDC) Slips Despite Plans to Highlight AI Data Storage Needs at the AI Infrastructure Summit", "description":"Western Digital (WDC) stock fell 2.75% despite plans to highlight AI data storage solutions at the upcoming AI Infrastructure Summit. The company will present findings from an IDC white paper indicating significant data growth driven by AI, with 61% of firms reporting over 25% increase last year. Senior VP Tim Rausch will discuss scalable storage needs for AI systems. Analysts maintain a 'Moderate Buy' consensus with an average price target of $680.94.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299076620", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789488884"}, {"id":"299060053", "title":"Storage Chip Stocks Diverge, Seagate Down 4%", "description":"Storage chip stocks showed mixed performance. Seagate(STX.US) fell 4%, Western Digital(WDC.US) dropped 2%, while Micron(MU.US) gained 1%. Divergent trends across sub-sectors as investors turn cautious.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299060053", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789480060"}, {"id":"299037377", "title":"Storage Chip Stocks Rise Premarket, Micron Up 0.86%, SanDisk Up 0.86%", "description":"Storage chip stocks climb in premarket trading. Micron(MU.US) up 0.86%, SanDisk up 0.86%, Western Digital up 0.81%. Sector extends recent strength with broad-based gains.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299037377", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789469265"}, {"id":"299014123", "title":"Storage Chip Stocks Edge Up in Overnight Trading, Micron Gains 0.71%", "description":"Storage chip stocks edged higher in overnight trading. Micron(MU.US) gained 0.71% to $930.61, SanDisk rose 0.54% to $1560.30. The sector continued its rebound from Monday's session weakness.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/299014123", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789458422"}, {"id":"298996481", "title":"Memory Chips Rise in Overnight Session, MU +0.72%, SNDK +0.77%, WDC +0.83%, STX +0.42%, MRAM +1.56%", "description":"Memory chip stocks rallied in the overnight session, with mainstream names all in the green. MRAM led gains at +1.56%, while MU and SNDK each rose over 0.7%. Derivative tickers showed mixed performance.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298996481", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789447590"}, {"id":"298989609", "title":"", "description":"Apple accepts Samsung's storage bid; two departments promote high-bandwidth flash memory and edge large model adaptation; Kioxia plans to raise $10 billion through a U.S. listing; TSMC faces tight capacity in advanced processes; TrendForce predicts an imbalance in NOR Flash supply and demand by 2026, with DDR5 prices remaining stable; institutions forecast global semiconductor revenue to reach $425 billion in Q2 2026. Micron and SanDisk compete for talent in South Korea, while Samsung responds to poaching; the Bank of Korea reviews stock market fluctuations", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298989609", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789441742"}, {"id":"298981120", "title":"Storage Chip Stocks Rise in Overnight Trading, Everspin Up 1.9%, Western Digital Up 0.9%", "description":"Storage chip stocks advanced across the board in overnight trading. Everspin led gains up 1.9%, Western Digital and Micron each rose nearly 1%. The sector extended daytime strength with HDD leaders and NAND producers moving higher together.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298981120", "comments_count":1, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789436812"}, {"id":"298968846", "title":"Storage chip stocks edge up, Western Digital up 1%, SanDisk little changed", "description":"Storage chip stocks edge higher in after-hours. Western Digital leads gains as sector rebounds from regular session losses.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298968846", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789426245"}, {"id":"298963445", "title":"Western Digital falls 5% after hours as AI leaders urge slower model development", "description":"WDC recovers 0.78% in after-hours to $430.28 after falling 4.53% in regular trading on AI sector profit-taking.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298963445", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789420222"}, {"id":"298960544", "title":"Western Digital Corp. Stock Underperforms Monday When Compared To Competitors", "description":"Western Digital Corp. (WDC) shares fell 4.53% to $426.94 on Monday, underperforming the broader market and its competitors like Seagate and NetApp. This marks the third consecutive day of losses for WDC, which is now trading 46.62% below its 52-week high. Trading volume remained below the 50-day average.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298960544", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789418202"}, {"id":"298960084", "title":"", "description":"On September 14, the U.S. stock memory chip and hardware supply chain index fell 6.21% to 190.76 points. Constituents generally declined, with Teradyne plunging 13.30%, Lam Research and SK Hynix ADR dropping over 7.6%, Micron Tech and Applied Materials falling more than 5.25%, and Sandisk, Western Digital, and Seagate Tech declining by 4.98%, 4.53%, and 2.97% respectively", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298960084", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789418057"}, {"id":"298958717", "title":"Western Digital Corp Stock (WDC) Closed Down by 4.53% on Sep 14: Facts Behind the Movement", "description":"Western Digital Corp (WDC) stock fell 4.53% on Sep 14, underperforming the Technology Equipment sector. The decline was driven by cautious market sentiment regarding AI infrastructure spending and concerns over potential share dilution from WDC's early redemption of convertible senior notes. Additional pressures included a secondary offering discount for SanDisk stakes and persistent insider selling. Despite technical oversold signals and bullish media sentiment, profit-taking dominated as investors reassessed valuation multiples ahead of macroeconomic updates.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298958717", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789417089"}, {"id":"298956876", "title":"Storage Chip Stocks Fall, MRAM Down 9%, Micron Down 5%", "description":"Storage chip stocks fell across the board. MRAM down 9%, Micron down 5%, SanDisk down 4%. Sector lacks catalysts as profit-taking emerges.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298956876", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789415297"}, {"id":"298946758", "title":"Storage Chip Stocks Decline Broadly, Everspin Down 8%, Micron Down 5%", "description":"Storage chip stocks fell broadly during regular trading. Everspin (MRAM) dropped 8%, Micron slid 5%, and SanDisk declined 5% as profit-taking swept the sector.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298946758", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789404456"}, {"id":"298944134", "title":"Western Digital falls 4% as AI leaders urge slowdown in model development", "description":"Western Digital fell 4% during regular trading as AI leaders' call to slow model development weighed on memory stocks", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298944134", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789402578"}, {"id":"298928872", "title":"Memory Chip Sector Plunges Intraday, MU Down Nearly 7%, MRAM Over 7%, SNDK Nearly 7%", "description":"The memory chip sector fell broadly during intraday trading on September 14. Mainstream stocks declined with MU down nearly 7%, MRAM over 7%, and SNDK, WDC, STX each dropping around 5%. Derivative MUD bucked the trend with gains.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298928872", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789393557"}, {"id":"298927888", "title":"US Stock Movement | Chip stocks generally decline, Intel (INTC.US) falls over 7%", "description":"On Monday, chip stocks fell broadly, with Intel (INTC.US) down over 7%, SK Hynix (SKHY.US) and Sandisk (SNDK.US) down 7%, Micron Technology (MU.US) and Seagate Tech (STX.US) down over 6%, Advanced Micro Devices (AMD.US) and Western Digital (WDC.US) down over 5%, Qualcomm (QCOM.US) and Broadcom (AVGO.US) down over 4%, and NVIDIA (NVDA.US) and Taiwan Semiconductor (TSM.US) down over 3%", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298927888", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789393318"}, {"id":"298927395", "title":"Western Digital drops 6% as AI leaders urge slower model development", "description":"Western Digital fell 6% during regular trading to $420.06 as AI leaders called for slowing frontier model development.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298927395", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789393021"}, {"id":"298886979", "title":"U.S. stock market movement | Storage stocks collectively fell before the market opened, with SK Hynix down over 6% and Sandisk down over 5%", "description":"Affected by the news of AI industry executives calling for a slowdown in the development pace of advanced models and strengthening safety measures, U.S. stocks of memory chips collectively fell in pre-market trading. SK Hynix dropped over 6%, Sandisk fell over 5%, and Micron Tech, Seagate Tech, and others also experienced varying degrees of decline", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298886979", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789373803"}, {"id":"298917972", "title":"The decline in the US stock storage sector has widened before the market opens, with major stocks falling over 6%", "description":"On September 14th, before the US stock market opened, the storage sector's decline expanded to a new intraday low, with major stocks such as SK Hynix, Seagate, Sandisk, Western Digital, and Micron Tech all dropping over 6%. During the same period, the three major US stock index futures also fell. The news was influenced by Anthropic CEO's call to slow down the development of cutting-edge AI models and introduce third-party assessments, which received support from OpenAI and Elon Musk", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298917972", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789388805"}, {"id":"298914613", "title":"Western Digital to redeem USD 109,505,000 of 3% convertible notes due 2028 on Nov. 16", "description":"Western Digital will redeem all outstanding $109.51 million principal of its 3.00% Convertible Senior Notes due 2028 on November 16, 2026, at 100% of principal plus accrued interest. Holders may convert notes until November 12, 2026, at a rate of 26.5231 shares per $1,000 principal. The company expects most holders to convert and plans to settle cash obligations up to the principal amount, with any excess value paid in shares.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298914613", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789387357"}, {"id":"298914422", "title":"", "description":"Western Digital Corporation will redeem all of its $109.5 million convertible preferred notes, with a coupon rate of 3.00%, maturing in 2028", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298914422", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789387298"}, {"id":"298914337", "title":"Why Is Micron Technology Stock Falling Monday?", "description":"Micron Technology (MU) stock fell over 5% in premarket trading, driven by broader sell-offs in memory and AI-linked stocks due to investor concerns regarding potential slowdowns in AI infrastructure spending. The decline coincided with drops in peers like Western Digital and SK hynix. Despite short-term momentum weakness, Micron remains in a long-term uptrend ahead of its September 30 earnings report, where analysts expect significant revenue growth. Analyst ratings remain largely positive, though price forecasts have been adjusted downward.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298914337", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789385532"}, {"id":"298908315", "title":"Pre-market hot trades in US stocks: Seagate Tech pre-market down 5.55%; Western Digital pre-market down 5.18%", "description":"Seagate Tech pre-market down 5.55%; Western Digital pre-market down 5.18%; Intercont pre-market up 56.36%; Scinai Immunotherapeutics pre-market up 54.82%; Elmet pre-market up 47.13%", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298908315", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789384120"}, {"id":"298908082", "title":"Western Digital's U.S. stock pre-market drops over 5%", "description":"Western Digital's stock fell over 5% in pre-market trading, currently reported at $424.44", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298908082", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789383971"}, {"id":"298905257", "title":"Memory Chips Pre-Market Decline Broadly, SNDK Down Nearly 5%, MU Down Nearly 5%", "description":"On Sept 14 pre-market, memory chip sector declined broadly with major names all lower. Micron and SanDisk both down nearly 5%, Western Digital down over 4%, Seagate and Everspin down nearly 4%.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298905257", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789382803"}, {"id":"298895151", "title":"Memory Stocks Slump Pre-Market, Micron Drops Over 5% as Calls to Slow AI R&D Hit Chip Market", "description":"US memory stocks slumped pre-market on September 14, with Micron, SanDisk, SK Hynix, Western Digital, and Seagate all dropping over 4%. This decline follows calls from leading AI executives, including Anthropic's Dario Amodei, to slow the pace of frontier AI model development due to safety concerns. Investors are reassessing AI capital expenditure expectations, impacting demand forecasts for high-performance storage like HBM and DRAM essential for AI servers.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298895151", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789377849"}, {"id":"298936051", "title":"U.S. Stock Market Movement | Optical Communication Concept Stocks Generally Decline, Nokia Drops Over 10%", "description":"On Monday, optical communication concept stocks generally fell, with Nokia, Corning, and Coherent dropping over 10%, Lumentum falling over 8%, Applied Optoelectronics and Credo Technology declining over 7%, and POET Technologies and Marvell Tech decreasing over 6%. On the news front, the three AI giants rarely called for a \"slowdown in the development of frontier models,\" raising market concerns about a reduction in capital expenditures for computing infrastructure, with optical communication being the most affected in the AI hardware supply chain. However, several analysts believe that the current statements remain at the \"verbal level,\" with no actual signals of capital expenditure cuts or order reductions yet materializing", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298936051", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789397643"}, {"id":"298886079", "title":"", "description":"In pre-market trading in the US, memory chip stocks generally fell. SK Hynix dropped more than 6%, Micron Tech fell nearly 5%, Western Digital declined close to 4%, and Sandisk slid over 5%", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298886079", "comments_count":1, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":3, "published_at":"1789373357"}, {"id":"298882852", "title":"Storage Chip Stocks Fall in Overnight Trading, SanDisk Down 5%, Micron Down 4%", "description":"Storage chip stocks declined in overnight trading. SanDisk fell over 5%, Micron dropped 4%, Seagate down 4%. Leveraged ETFs showed amplified losses.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298882852", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789372009"}, {"id":"298867069", "title":"Memory Chips Slide in Overnight Session, MU Falls Nearly 4%, SNDK Drops Over 4%", "description":"The memory chip sector declined broadly during overnight trading, with mainstream names like MU and SNDK falling over 3%, while derivative tickers MUD and SNDQ surged more than 8%.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298867069", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789361156"}, {"id":"298861711", "title":"U.S. stock night market volatility: Western Digital fell 3.06% in the night market, facing a double blow from UBS's downgrade and equity dilution, highlighting the risk of overvaluation", "description":"Western Digital fell 3.06% in after-hours trading; SanDisk fell 4.04% in after-hours trading, with a transaction volume of 200 million USD; Apple fell 1.10% in after-hours trading, with a transaction volume of 30.37 million USD; Dell Technologies-C fell 1.63% in after-hours trading, with a transaction volume of 25.15 million USD", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298861711", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789356794"}, {"id":"298815837", "title":"Top 5 US Stock Gainers/Losers (>100B) (9.11)", "description":"Dell Tech(DELL) rose 11.98%, with a trading turnover 8.1 Billion USD, and a year-to-date rose 354.8%. HDFC Bank(HDB) rose 6.87%, with a trading turnover 629.0 Million USD, and a year-to-date fell 35%. Seagate Tech(STX) fell 3.73%, with a trading turnover 3.2 Billion USD, and a year-to-date rose 201.7%. Sandisk(SNDK) fell 3.5%, with a trading turnover 15.4 Billion USD, and a year-to-date rose 588.1%.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298815837", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789250451"}, {"id":"298814032", "title":"Large Cap Stocks To Follow Now - September 12th", "description":"MarketBeat's stock screener identifies Micron Technology, NVIDIA, Invesco QQQ, Apple, and SanDisk as the top five large-cap stocks to watch on September 12th. These selections are based on having the highest dollar trading volume among large-cap stocks recently. Large-cap stocks, typically valued at $10 billion or more, are viewed as established entities with potentially lower volatility compared to smaller firms.", "url":"https://longbridge.cn/news/298814032", "comments_count":0, "likes_count":0, "shares_count":0, "published_at":"1789239719"}]}}
